{
  "schema": "trial/1",
  "trial": "P-73",
  "question": "What does the Checks API take of one neutral check run's annotations: how many in one request, how many in all over updates, the longest message kept whole, and does it keep an annotation on a path outside the pull request's diff, or one with no line?",
  "pass": "Written before the run, in issue 1030 at 2026-11-20T18:18Z, nothing having run (trial TA4 of decision 0224's plan): in the canary, on a pull request of the trial's own that changes p73/a.py (canary pull request 132, branch trial/p-73, head 410baec), a workflow with its own GITHUB_TOKEN, granted checks write, makes completed neutral check runs: 1, 50 and 51 annotations; three updates of 50 more to the run of 50, then its annotations listed; a message of 65,536 and of 65,535 ASCII characters, each read back; an annotation on README.md, which the change does not touch; one with no start_line or end_line. The writer is GitHub Actions' App, not the Factory's: the annotation limits are the Checks API's, the same for every App, and this session may not mint the Factory App's token. Each answer was written to a file in the job and redacted there by software-factory's tools.redact_trial at d53baceb before it was uploaded. Pass: each is answered by what GitHub returned and recorded; it fails only if an answer cannot be read. Result, of what this file's own exchanges hold: a message of 65,536 ASCII characters is taken, 201, and read back cut to 65,535, with no word of it; one of 65,535 is taken and read back whole; each such message is written here as '<N times the letter m>', N as counted on the redacted answer, to keep the fixture small, and a limit on a message of characters of more than one byte was not asked. An annotation on README.md, which the change does not touch, is taken, 201, with its blob_href at the head; the list of that run's annotations, asked about two seconds after its create, answered 404 Not Found, and P-73.json holds the Maintainer's read a minute later that lists it. Why that list answered 404 GitHub does not say: a read made just after a write may miss the run it names. The Factory's own cap on a message, 8,000 characters (adapters/advice.py), sits within the 65,535 kept whole. Passed. What this file keeps (2026-11-21, to fit the review's size bound): exchanges 9 to 14 of the trial's 18, in the order they happened. P-73.json holds the rest but those owed in P-73.fifty.json (the create of the run of 50 and its first update) and P-73.updates.json (the second and third updates).",
